What:		/sys/devices/platform/soc/38a00000.nand-controller/image
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	6.14
Contact:	Kailash <kailash.sudhakar@gmail.com>
Description:
		(RW) The file that makes up the "nandlinux" disk on the
		iPod touch 2G NAND (n72-yaftl). Writing takes one command per
		line: "new PARTITION" starts an extent list in the named
		partition; "ext START COUNT" adds the file's next extent
		(512-byte sectors in the partition, whole 4 KiB blocks, in
		file order); "commit" checks the list and creates the disk
		read-only; "rw" allows writing (unless the fmss ftl_write
		module parameter is 0). Reading returns the state: a first
		line "state none|ro|rw" (followed by " failed" after a
		failure), then lines "extents", "sectors", "buffered",
		"read_sectors", "written_sectors", "flushes", "merged_pages"
		and "ftl_" counters (free_blocks, user_blocks, index_blocks,
		stale_index, user_pages, gc_pages, gc_blocks, index_pages,
		erases, usn), each as "<name> <value>".

What:		/sys/devices/platform/soc/38a00000.nand-controller/ftl_test
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	6.14
Contact:	Kailash <kailash.sudhakar@gmail.com>
Description:
		(RW) Test hook, present only when
		CONFIG_BLK_DEV_N72_NAND_DEBUG is enabled. Writing
		"LPN COUNT SEED" writes COUNT (up to 4096) test pages from
		logical page LPN and reads each back; "v LPN COUNT SEED" only
		reads and compares. Only logical pages above those exposed to
		iOS are accepted (-ERANGE otherwise), and writing needs the
		fmss ftl_write parameter (-EPERM otherwise). Reading returns
		the page counts and free blocks, and the result of the last
		test.

What:		/sys/devices/platform/soc/38a00000.nand-controller/ftl_check
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	6.14
Contact:	Kailash <kailash.sudhakar@gmail.com>
Description:
		(RO) Test hook, present only when
		CONFIG_BLK_DEV_N72_NAND_DEBUG is enabled. Reports what
		writing would start from without writing anything: open
		blocks, and how many index pages disagree with the map built
		by the scan.
